   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Exodus 3:7-8, what four things does God say he has seen, heard, known and come down to do for his people?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Exodus 12:26-27, what are parents to tell their children when they ask about the Passover, and why might Israel have built a question into the ritual?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does Exodus 20:2 connect the commandments to the rescue from Egypt? What difference does it make that God saves first and then gives the law?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/the-exodus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:the-exodus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul calls Christ \"our Passover\" (1 Corinthians 5:7) and says the wilderness events \"happened to them by way of example\" (1 Corinthians 10:11). Where do you see your own story in Israel's — both the rescue and the grumbling afterwards?"
  }
